{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# 🧭 Networx program — macro model (top-down)\n\n**Vision:** a cohesive set of **open-source components grounded in a shared ontological & semantic language** that puts strategic cyber-risk decisions in the hands of those most qualified — *business operators, not sales folk*. **Compliance-as-code** as the foundational tenet of digitally transforming an industry that desperately needs it.\n\n_Derived from the owner's hand-written narrative + three slides (27 Jul 2026). The two bottom-up maps (wayfinder decisions, session corpus) hang UNDER these boxes — see the ⬇ nodes._","x":-1400,"y":-1150,"width":2820,"height":240,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"asis","type":"text","text":"## 🔥 The problem (as-is customer journey)\n\nMost customers are **overwhelmed by cyber risk**. Today every step is manual, disconnected, low-maturity:\n\n1. **Risk assessment** — manual interviews + industry research; controls/policy rarely effective\n2. **Quantify $ of risk** — extreme difficulty; Open FAIR isn't truly *open*; insurer loss data hard to get → *TASK-1.10 FAIR*\n3. **Business impact analysis** — clients can't articulate the financial impost\n4. **Asset inventory** — can't protect what you can't see (automated scans where possible)\n5. **Visual threat models** — current vs target state\n6. **Vuln assessment / pentest / identity**\n7. **Control selection** — min compliance + risk appetite → **.docx/.xlsx outputs** *(the NCF product today)*\n8. **Train & educate** on controls + capture metrics\n9. **Audit** (internal/external) → board memo for decisions & resourcing\n10. **3rd-party risk** — unvalidated questionnaires → supply-chain attacks\n11. **SecOps** (SIEM/EDR/FW/CASB/VM) — disparate, multi-party, vanity metrics, negligible risk reduction\n12. **Tooling** — mediocre point solutions ↔ overwhelming enterprise ↔ OSS\n13. **Vendor FUD** — no skin in the game; buyers can't validate efficacy; no shared language\n14. Every product has a **black-box AI layer** nobody can prove / benchmark / adapt","x":-1520,"y":-860,"width":560,"height":1040,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"msp","type":"text","text":"## 🏢 Networx MSP\n_The 20+ yr business being digitally transformed; **low operational maturity**._\n\n**Service Delivery Areas** (your slide ↓):\n- Service Desk / Support — reactive; the primary way clients judge support\n- Professional Services — implementations, moves/adds/changes, billable\n- Centralised Services — proactive: patch, AV, monitoring, backup/DR, cloud\n- Network Administration — standardisation, technical risk\n- Business Relationship / vCIO — tech planning, budgeting, business risk\n\n_The **context & install base** — mostly Ring-1 reality, not build scope, but the substrate everything transforms._","x":-900,"y":-860,"width":540,"height":320,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cyber","type":"text","text":"## 🛡️ Cyber Security Practice\n_What you were hired (CSO) to build — but op-maturity / tech-debt / competency gaps meant you've been acting **COO**. **Function × Capability** (your slide ↓)._\n\n**Functions:** GRC · Security Engineering · Testing & Validation · Security Operations · Research & Analysis · DFIR · Education & Training\n\n_The **domain / product spine.** The as-is journey (left) is exactly what this practice, done right, turns into cohesive components._","x":-320,"y":-860,"width":540,"height":320,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"ai","type":"text","text":"## 🤖 AI Practice\n_A **distinct, independently-viable capability** — not subordinate to Cyber. It **builds** the Cyber Practice via dogfooding, and sells to non-cyber clients (finance, commodity, construction). May go to market **first**._\n\n**7 pillars:** GRC · Problem discovery & advisory · AI engineering · Testing & validation · AI operations · Research & analysis · Education & training\n\n⚠️ Needs its **own problem-shape box** (why clients struggle to operationalise AI) — from `ai-practice/`. **AI GRC ≠ Cyber GRC.**","x":260,"y":-860,"width":540,"height":320,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"nom","type":"text","text":"## ⚙️ New Operating Model / Strategy (EOS)\n_The **substrate that underpins all three** practices — not a 4th silo._\n\n- **EOS** — align strategy/leadership/personnel on **True North**: People · Strategy · Execution · Cash\n- Collaboration, info-sharing, corporate values, strategy-on-a-page\n- **Guardrails over governance**; distilled from Collins/Harnish/Lencioni/Sinek/Ries\n- The gated-experimentation framework is **one component**\n\n_Machine-readable data + compliance-as-code. The vault/substrate + TASK-1.1 live here._","x":840,"y":-860,"width":560,"height":320,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"img_msp","type":"file","file":"canvas/reference/traditional-msp.png","x":-900,"y":-510,"width":535,"height":340},
		{"id":"img_cyber","type":"file","file":"canvas/reference/security-practice.png","x":-320,"y":-510,"width":540,"height":291},
		{"id":"img_ai","type":"file","file":"canvas/reference/ai-practice.png","x":260,"y":-510,"width":540,"height":335},
		{"id":"nom_themes","type":"text","text":"### Operating-model building blocks\n(from `llm-biases/ian specific/` — gated experimentation)\n\n- **Gated process:** problem → experiment → project (staged gates)\n- **Thinking discipline:** problem framing · hypotheses & falsifiability · innovation accounting\n- **Templates:** information paper · experiment proposal · project proposal\n- **Anti-patterns register** + the critical-thinking / LLM-slop guardrails\n\n→ digest: `research/macro-inputs/operating-model-digest.md`\n→ ingest `TASK-2.14`","x":840,"y":-510,"width":560,"height":340,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"attach_cyber","type":"text","text":"### ⬇ What hangs here — the NCF product\nThe **wayfinder decision map (TASK-1)** is the buildable product under this box (and the New Operating Model):\nNCF control framework → document factory (.docx/.xlsx + per-client token model) → FAIR risk-quant → the 20+ suite bookshelf.\n\nThis is where the as-is journey's steps 1-9 get **productised as cohesive components**.\n\n→ [[wayfinder-map.canvas]]","x":-320,"y":-140,"width":540,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"attach_ai","type":"text","text":"### ⬇ What hangs here — the Learnings corpus\nThe **session corpus (TASK-2)** — 14 prior sessions + dogfooding evidence, the Learnings domain — is the proof base for \"prove it as we sell it.\"\n\nEvery pillar's *dogfooded* cell should point at a real session here.\n\n→ [[session-corpus-map.canvas]]","x":260,"y":-140,"width":540,"height":240,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"sandbox","type":"text","text":"## 🧪 Sandbox (adjacent)\n_Experimentation that doesn't yet have to fit a top-down box._\n\nMaps to the **monorepo control-plane** idea (TASK-1.1 fog): pull sibling code into referenced subdirs; a control plane to start/stop apps for exploration; single backlog.","x":840,"y":-140,"width":560,"height":220,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"linkages","type":"text","text":"## 🔗 Cross-box linkages (corrected after review)\n\n- **Cyber GRC ≠ AI GRC** — different domains. AI GRC = the operating model of AI usage (which models, observability, disclosure), **not** the NCF engine.\n- **as-is \"$ risk\" ↔ FAIR ↔ insurance** — real, but **FAIR is a deep domain, NOT elevated** (snake-oil risk if done badly).\n- **AI Testing/Validation ↔ black-box-AI** — provability differentiator → build an **agent harness + observability** layer early (upstream).\n- **New Operating Model (EOS) ↔ everything** — the connective substrate, not a silo.\n- **MSP ↔ both practices** — tenant-zero + first customer of Cyber *and* AI; concurrent workstreams.\n\n_Detailed branch-to-branch mapping = later._","x":-1520,"y":210,"width":1360,"height":300,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"legend","type":"text","text":"## Legend / provenance\n- **Boxes** = your top-down model (hand-written narrative + 3 slides, 27 Jul 2026).\n- **Slides embedded as your originals** (`canvas/reference/*.png`) — the source of truth for each box's decomposition.\n- **🔥 as-is journey** (left) = the problem; **🧭 vision** (top) = the destination; the four boxes are how you get there.\n- **Bottom-up maps hang underneath** via [[wayfinder-map.canvas]] (the NCF build) and [[session-corpus-map.canvas]] (the Learnings corpus).\n- **Comprehensive notes:** `program-map/MACRO-PROGRAM-STRUCTURE.md`\n- Deep digests of the two new folders: `research/macro-inputs/` (AI Practice deck, operating-model framework).","x":-120,"y":210,"width":1520,"height":300,"color":"3"}
	],
